config BR2_PACKAGE_STYX_PISPBE
	bool "styx-pispbe"
	depends on BR2_LINUX_KERNEL
	help
	  Styx's build of the PiSP back end driver (pisp_be): the image
	  kernel's own driver with a cheaper per-job config write (about
	  7 us of CPU per job instead of about 120 us). It starts every back
	  end job about 0.11 ms sooner; the hardware sees the same register
	  values. Installed to /lib/modules/<release>/updates/, where it
	  takes precedence over the kernel's own pisp-be.ko; the kernel
	  itself is not changed. For Styx images.

	  The build fails when the kernel's own pisp_be sources are not the
	  ones the Styx driver was made from (re-import them:
	  kernel-modules/pispbe).

comment "styx-pispbe needs a Linux kernel to be built"
	depends on !BR2_LINUX_KERNEL
